<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borommarachathirat I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1370–1388</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Khun Luang Pa-ngua, Khun Luang Pa-ngua of Suphanburi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borommarachathirat I, earlier Khun Luang Pa-ngua, ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suphanburi">Suphanburi</a>, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> from 1370 to 1388. A brother-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramathibodi-i">U Thong</a>, the founder of Ayutthaya, he seized the throne from U Thong's son Ramesuan and established the Suphannaphum dynasty in power. He campaigned repeatedly against Sukhothai, which became a tributary of Ayutthaya in 1378.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borommarachathirat-i.jpg" alt="Borommarachathirat I" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FrameHotep · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borommarachathirat_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
